    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build succeeds and all tests pass. The audit log confirms the behavior: `membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M27` \u2014 the year segment is now `27`, the fiscal year for a 2026-08-14 registration date (August is on/after 1 July, so it rolls into FY2027).\n\nLet me verify the full picture of what I implemented:\n\n**Summary of changes**\n\nThe fiscal year starts 1 July, so a date on or after 1 July belongs to the *following* calendar year's fiscal year (e.g. `2026-08-14` \u2192 fiscal year 2027 \u2192 `FY27`). All date-derived values now use the business-day-adjusted `registrationDate` that is already persisted on the owner.\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the new read-only `fiscalYear` field (`FY<YY>`) to the Owner schema, and updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to reflect the fiscal-year basis.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 `membershipNumber(...)` now derives its `M<YY>` segment from the registration date's fiscal year (via a new `fiscalYear(LocalDate)` helper) rather than the calendar year.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`**:\n   - Added the `fiscalYear` mapping + `fiscalYear(Owner)` method returning `FY<YY>` (null when no registration date).\n   - Replaced the day-based `tenureDays` (`> 365`) with `tenureFiscalYears` \u2014 the count of elapsed fiscal years (current FY minus registration FY) \u2014 gating the tenure membership points on more than one elapsed fiscal year.\n   - Removed the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import.\n\nThe single acceptance test `coreReturnsFiscalYear` (asserting `fiscalYear` matches `FY\\d{2}`) passes, and the full suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
